  <!-- Msgcore is consumed as an include path plus an import library, never as a
       linked project output: LinkLibraryDependencies is false, so the explicit
       Msgcore.lib in <AdditionalDependencies> stays the one that is linked. The
       reference exists purely to ORDER the build, so a stale Msgcore.lib can no
       longer be linked silently by building this project first.

       ShouldUnsetParentConfigurationAndPlatform (set false just above, beside
       UserMacros) IS LOAD-BEARING FOR THIS REFERENCE, and the default of true
       corrupts the shared lib tree. A solution build sets it true, which strips
       Configuration and Platform from the global properties handed to a
       referenced project so that each one picks its own default. Msgcore then
       evaluates MSCS\Directory.Build.props with $(Platform) and $(Configuration)
       still empty, and that file appends the platform and configuration to
       $(WDMSCS_LIB) only when BOTH are set. The result: Msgcore wrote its import
       library to MSCS\lib\Msgcore.lib (the un-suffixed root, which is the very
       failure Directory.Build.props exists to prevent) while its DLL still went
       to out\Win32\Debug\. Worse, under -t:Rebuild the Clean first DELETED the
       correct MSCS\lib\Win32\Debug\Msgcore.lib, so the next link failed with
       LNK1104 on a file that had been present all along.

       SetConfiguration/SetPlatform below are kept as the explicit statement of
       which variant is wanted; on their own they did NOT fix this, because the
       unsetting happens regardless of them.

       If this reference is ever removed, keep a check that fails the build when
       $(WDMSCS_LIB)\Msgcore.lib is missing. Silence is the defect being fixed
       here, not the ordering by itself. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Msgcore\Msgcore(2022).vcxproj">
      <Project>{c1e33b10-d6ce-44be-8f98-080196bc682b}</Project>
      <SetConfiguration>Configuration=$(Configuration)</SetConfiguration>
      <SetPlatform>Platform=$(Platform)</SetPlatform>
      <LinkLibraryDependencies>false</LinkLibraryDependencies>
      <UseLibraryDependencyInputs>false</UseLibraryDependencyInputs>
    </ProjectReference>
  </ItemGroup>
